<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!-- One value, one place — but only for values that are genuinely repeated.

       This dictionary is deliberately tiny. The page has ~30 corner radii and paddings that each appear once,
       and a token nobody asserts is decoration: it adds a lookup and a name without removing a decision. What
       lives here is what appears in several files at once, where a change in one place and not the other is a
       real bug the eye will not catch: the chat column's width is declared in the transcript, the composer and
       the two decision surfaces; the frame radius is the composer's and the picture viewer's.

       Theme-independent on purpose, so these sit at the dictionary root rather than in a ThemeDictionaries
       block: a metric that changed with the theme would be two numbers pretending to be one.

       The C# side that builds surfaces in code (the decision host, the plan option rows, the inspector) reads
       the same numbers from AxmolHub.HubMetrics, and a shell assertion pins the two sides equal; that
       assertion, not this file, is what keeps them in step. -->

  <x:Double x:Key="Hub.Column.MaxWidth">820</x:Double>

  <CornerRadius x:Key="Hub.Radius.Frame">14</CornerRadius>
  <CornerRadius x:Key="Hub.Radius.Card">12</CornerRadius>
  <CornerRadius x:Key="Hub.Radius.Pill">15</CornerRadius>

  <Thickness x:Key="Hub.Space.Row">10</Thickness>

</ResourceDictionary>
